{"tool_name":"cytofkit","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"cytofkit","home":"http://bioconductor.org/packages/release/bioc/html/cytofkit.html","license":"Artistic-2.0","summary":"An integrated mass cytometry data analysis pipeline that enables simultaneous illustration of cellular diversity and progression.","addition_date":"2017-01-17T14:59:07Z","last_update_date":"2019-01-11T01:04:26Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool","Library"],"version":["1.6.1"],"collections":["BioConductor"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:cytofkit","credit":[{"email":"Chen_Jinmiao@immunol.a-star.edu.sg","name":"Jinmiao Chen","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]},{"email":"chen_hao@immunol.a-star.edu.sg","name":"Hao Chen","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]},{"email":"enewell@fredhutch.org","name":"Evan Newell","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Contributor"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["User manual"],"url":"http://bioconductor.org/packages/release/bioc/html/cytofkit.html"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"input":[{"data":{"term":"Mass spectrometry data","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_2536"},"format":[{"term":"Binary format","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_2333"}]}],"operation":[{"term":"Clustering","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3432"},{"term":"Spectral analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3214"},{"term":"Visualisation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0337"}],"output":[{"data":{"term":"Plot","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_2884"},"format":[{"term":"Binary format","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_2333"},{"term":"Image format","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3547"},{"term":"Matrix format","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3033"},{"term":"Textual format","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_2330"}]},{"data":{"term":"Report","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_2048"},"format":[{"term":"Binary format","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_2333"},{"term":"Image format","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3547"},{"term":"Matrix format","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3033"},{"term":"Textual format","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_2330"}]}]}],"name":"cytofkit","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"bioconductor_import","publication":[{"doi":"10.1016/j.celrep.2015.05.022","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 2015 The Authors.Single-cell analysis technologies such as mass cytometry allow for measurements of cellular heterogeneity with unprecedented dimensionality. Here, we applied dimensionality reduction and automated clustering methods on human T helper (T<inf>H</inf>) cells derived from peripheral blood and tonsils, which showed differential cell composition and extensive T<inf>H</inf> cell heterogeneity. Notably, this analysis revealed numerous subtypes of follicular helper T (T<inf>FH</inf>) cells that followed a continuum spanning both blood and tonsils. Furthermore, we identified tonsillar CXCR5<sup>lo</sup>PD-1<sup>lo</sup>CCR7<sup>lo</sup> T<inf>FH</inf> cells expressing interferon-\u03b3 (IFN-\u03b3), interleukin-17 (IL-17), or Foxp3, indicating that T<inf>FH</inf> cells exhibit diverse functional capacities within extrafollicular stages. Regression analysis demonstrated that CXCR5<sup>lo</sup>PD-1<sup>-</sup> and CXCR5<sup>lo</sup>PD-1<sup>lo</sup> cells accumulate during childhood in secondary lymphoid organs, supporting previous findings that these subsets represent memory T<inf>FH</inf> cells. This study provides an in-depth comparison of human blood and tonsillar T<inf>FH</inf> cells and outlines a general approach for subset discovery and hypothesizing of cellular progressions. In this study, Wong et al. use mass cytometry to comprehensively probe the phenotypic and functional profiles of human blood- and tonsil-derived CD4<sup>+</sup> T cells. This analysis uncovers multiple subtypes of T<inf>FH</inf> cells spanning blood and tonsils. Regression analysis reveals that during childhood, memory T<inf>FH</inf> cells accumulate with age.","authors":[{"name":"Anicete R."},{"name":"Chen J."},{"name":"De Lafaille M.A.C."},{"name":"Kiaang H.T.K."},{"name":"Lin W."},{"name":"Narayanan S."},{"name":"Newell E.W."},{"name":"Poidinger M."},{"name":"Wong M.T."}],"citationCount":86,"date":"2015-01-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Cell Reports","title":"Mapping the Diversity of Follicular Helper T Cells in Human Blood and Tonsils Using High-Dimensional Mass Cytometry Analysis"},"pmid":"26074076","type":["Primary"]}],"topic":[{"term":"Data mining","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3473"},{"term":"Data visualisation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0092"},{"term":"Laboratory techniques","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3361"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"cytofkit","home":"https://bio.tools/cytofkit","license":"Artistic-2.0","version":"1.6.1","summary":"An integrated mass cytometry data analysis pipeline that enables simultaneous illustration of cellular diversity and progression.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:cytofkit:1.6.1/cmd/bioconductor.org","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"sourcecode":{"interpreted":true}},"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"documentation":{"manual":true},"license":{"open_source":true,"osi":true},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_count":76,"citations":[{"count":1,"year":"2023"},{"count":2,"year":"2024"},{"count":2,"year":"2026"},{"count":3,"year":"2025"},{"count":5,"year":"2021"},{"count":5,"year":"2022"},{"count":9,"year":"2016"},{"count":10,"year":"2017"},{"count":10,"year":"2019"},{"count":14,"year":"2018"},{"count":15,"year":"2020"}],"doi":"10.1016/j.celrep.2015.05.022","pmid":"26074076","ref_count":0,"refs":[],"title":"Mapping the Diversity of Follicular Helper T Cells in Human Blood and Tonsils Using High-Dimensional Mass Cyto